; A variable that only a make mentions is a fresh unknown, a new one for each
; firing: the two (item ?) rows hold two unknowns.  An unknown is not a name:
; it may still equal any term, so once an item exists, (item c) is no longer
; known absent, and watch can fire only before the first item.  tcalc@0.1 has
; no names that no other term equals; rho's new is refused (refused_rho_new).
(step one)
(seed)
(seed)
(rule grow (take (seed)) (make (item $n)))
(rule watch (absent (item c)) (absent (watched)) (make (watched)))
